\page \pard\f0\fs28\b\sl360\slmult0\sa180 \cf1 Problem 5 Weather station analyzer\par
\pard\f0\fs20\b0\sl260\slmult0\sa120 \cf1 p5_Alfaro_Jorge.py\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf3 """Problem 5: weather observations, statistics and outliers.\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf3 Input is headerless CSV: station,date,temperature. Dates use\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf3 %I:%M:%S %p %m/%d/%Y. Output CSV contains station,min,max,mean.\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf3 Run: python p5_Alfaro_Jorge.py observations.csv statistics.csv\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf3 """\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf5 import\cf1  csv\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf5 from\cf1  datetime \cf5 import\cf1  datetime\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf5 import\cf1  sys\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1 DATE_FORMAT = \cf3 "%I:%M:%S %p %m/%d/%Y"\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1 Observations = dict[str, list[tuple[str, float]]]\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1 Statistics = dict[str, tuple[float, float, float]]\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf5 def\cf1  read_observations(filename: str) -> tuple[Observations, list[tuple[int, str]]]:\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1     \cf3 """Read valid observations in chronological order and report bad lines.\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf3     The first valid observation for a station and parsed date wins.\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf3     File-access errors propagate to the caller.\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf3     """\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1     observations, errors, seen = \{\}, [], set()\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1     \cf5 with\cf1  open(filename, encoding=\cf3 "utf-8"\cf1 ) \cf5 as\cf1  file:\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1         \cf5 for\cf1  line_number, line \cf5 in\cf1  enumerate(file, \cf4 1\cf1 ):\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1             \cf5 try\cf1 :\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1                 row = next(csv.reader([line], strict=\cf5 True\cf1 ))\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1                 \cf5 if\cf1  len(row) != \cf4 3\cf1 :\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1                     \cf5 raise\cf1  ValueError(\cf3 "Expected station,date,temperature."\cf1 )\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1                 station, date, text = (field.strip() \cf5 for\cf1  field \cf5 in\cf1  row)\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1                 \cf5 if\cf1  \cf5 not\cf1  station:\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1                     \cf5 raise\cf1  ValueError(\cf3 "Station cannot be empty."\cf1 )\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1                 timestamp = datetime.strptime(date, DATE_FORMAT)\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1                 temperature = float(text)\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1                 \cf5 if\cf1  \cf5 not\cf1  -\cf4 100.0\cf1  <= temperature <= \cf4 150.0\cf1 :\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1                     \cf5 raise\cf1  ValueError(\cf3 "Temperature must be between -100 and 150."\cf1 )\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1                 key = (station, timestamp)\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1                 \cf5 if\cf1  key \cf5 in\cf1  seen:\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1                     \cf5 raise\cf1  ValueError(\cf3 "Duplicate station/date observation."\cf1 )\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1                 seen.add(key)\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1                 observations.setdefault(station, []).append((date, temperature))\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1             \cf5 except\cf1  (ValueError, csv.Error) \cf5 as\cf1  error:\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1                 errors.append((line_number, str(error)))\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1     \cf5 for\cf1  records \cf5 in\cf1  observations.values():\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1         records.sort(key=\cf5 lambda\cf1  item: datetime.strptime(item[\cf4 0\cf1 ], DATE_FORMAT))\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1     \cf5 return\cf1  observations, errors\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf5 def\cf1  station_statistics(observations: Observations) -> Statistics:\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1     \cf3 """Map each nonempty station to its minimum, maximum and mean."""\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1     statistics = \{\}\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1     \cf5 for\cf1  station, records \cf5 in\cf1  observations.items():\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1         \cf5 if\cf1  records:\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1             temperatures = [temperature \cf5 for\cf1  _, temperature \cf5 in\cf1  records]\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1             statistics[station] = (min(temperatures), max(temperatures),\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1                                    sum(temperatures) / len(temperatures))\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1     \cf5 return\cf1  statistics\par
\page \pard\f0\fs28\b\sl360\slmult0\sa180 \cf1 Problem 5 Weather station analyzer continued\par
\pard\f0\fs20\b0\sl260\slmult0\sa120 \cf1 p5_Alfaro_Jorge.py\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf5 def\cf1  station_outliers(observations: Observations) -> dict[str, tuple[str, float, float]]:\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1     \cf3 """Map stations whose latest value exceeds their mean to (date, value, mean).\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf3     Observations must be chronologically sorted, as read_observations returns.\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf3     """\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1     statistics = station_statistics(observations)\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1     \cf5 return\cf1  \{station: (*records[-\cf4 1\cf1 ], statistics[station][\cf4 2\cf1 ])\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1             \cf5 for\cf1  station, records \cf5 in\cf1  observations.items()\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1             \cf5 if\cf1  records \cf5 and\cf1  records[-\cf4 1\cf1 ][\cf4 1\cf1 ] > statistics[station][\cf4 2\cf1 ]\}\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf5 def\cf1  write_statistics(filename: str, statistics: Statistics) -> \cf5 None\cf1 :\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1     \cf3 """Write stations alphabetically, with all numbers to one decimal place."""\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1     \cf5 with\cf1  open(filename, \cf3 "w"\cf1 , newline=\cf3 ""\cf1 , encoding=\cf3 "utf-8"\cf1 ) \cf5 as\cf1  file:\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1         writer = csv.writer(file)\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1         writer.writerow([\cf3 "station"\cf1 , \cf3 "min"\cf1 , \cf3 "max"\cf1 , \cf3 "mean"\cf1 ])\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1         \cf5 for\cf1  station \cf5 in\cf1  sorted(statistics):\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1             writer.writerow([station, *(f"\{value:.1f\}"\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1                                         \cf5 for\cf1  value \cf5 in\cf1  statistics[station])])\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf5 def\cf1  main() -> int:\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1     \cf3 """Read command-line paths, report results and handle file-access errors."""\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1     print(\cf3 "Student: Jorge Alfaro | FAU ID: Z23697022 | Problem 5"\cf1 )\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1     \cf5 if\cf1  len(sys.argv) != \cf4 3\cf1 :\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1         print(f"Usage: \{sys.argv[\cf4 0\cf1 ]\} INPUT.csv OUTPUT.csv", file=sys.stderr)\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1         \cf5 return\cf1  \cf4 1\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1     \cf5 try\cf1 :\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1         observations, errors = read_observations(sys.argv[\cf4 1\cf1 ])\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1         statistics = station_statistics(observations)\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1         print(\cf3 "Statistics (minimum, maximum, mean)"\cf1 )\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1         \cf5 for\cf1  station \cf5 in\cf1  sorted(statistics):\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1             values = \cf3 ", "\cf1 .join(f"\{value:.1f\}" \cf5 for\cf1  value \cf5 in\cf1  statistics[station])\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1             print(f"\{station\}: \{values\}")\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1         print(\cf3 "Outliers (date, temperature, mean)"\cf1 )\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1         outliers = station_outliers(observations)\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1         \cf5 for\cf1  station, (date, value, mean) \cf5 in\cf1  sorted(outliers.items()):\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1             print(f"\{station\}: \{date\}, \{value:.1f\}, \{mean:.1f\}")\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1         \cf5 for\cf1  line, message \cf5 in\cf1  errors:\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1             print(f"Rejected line \{line\}: \{message\}")\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1         write_statistics(sys.argv[\cf4 2\cf1 ], statistics)\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1         \cf5 return\cf1  \cf4 0\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1     \cf5 except\cf1  (OSError, UnicodeError) \cf5 as\cf1  error:\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1         print(f"Could not access the weather data: \{error\}", file=sys.stderr)\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1         \cf5 return\cf1  \cf4 1\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf5 if\cf1  __name__ == \cf3 "__main__"\cf1 :\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1     sys.exit(main())\par
\page \pard\f0\fs28\b\sl360\slmult0\sa180 \cf1 Problem 5 Unit tests\par
\pard\f0\fs20\b0\sl260\slmult0\sa120 \cf1 test_p5.py\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf3 """Run with: python -m unittest -v test_p5.py (from this directory)."""\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf5 from\cf1  contextlib \cf5 import\cf1  redirect_stderr, redirect_stdout\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf5 import\cf1  importlib.util\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf5 import\cf1  io\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf5 from\cf1  pathlib \cf5 import\cf1  Path\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf5 from\cf1  tempfile \cf5 import\cf1  TemporaryDirectory\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf5 import\cf1  unittest\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf5 from\cf1  unittest.mock \cf5 import\cf1  patch\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf2 # Locate the solution even after its student-name placeholders are replaced.\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1 SOURCE = next(Path(__file__).parent.glob(\cf3 "p5_*.py"\cf1 ))\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1 SPEC = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(\cf3 "weather"\cf1 , SOURCE)\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1 weather = importlib.util.module_from_spec(SPEC)\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1 SPEC.loader.exec_module(weather)\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf5 class\cf1  WeatherTests(unittest.TestCase):\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1     \cf3 """Exercise input validation, calculations, output and error handling."""\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1     \cf5 def\cf1  setUp(self) -> \cf5 None\cf1 :\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1         \cf3 """Create an isolated directory for each test."""\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1         self.folder = TemporaryDirectory()\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1         self.addCleanup(self.folder.cleanup)\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1         self.input = Path(self.folder.name) / \cf3 "input.csv"\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1         self.output = Path(self.folder.name) / \cf3 "output.csv"\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1     \cf5 def\cf1  read(self, content: str) -> tuple:\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1         \cf3 """Write a fixture and return its parsed observations and errors."""\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1         self.input.write_text(content, encoding=\cf3 "utf-8"\cf1 )\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1         \cf5 return\cf1  weather.read_observations(str(self.input))\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1     \cf5 def\cf1  test_several_stations_and_negative_temperatures(self) -> \cf5 None\cf1 :\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1         \cf3 """Keep valid observations for distinct stations, including negatives."""\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1         observations, errors = self.read(\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1             \cf3 "North,09:00:00 AM 01/01/2026,-12.5\\n"\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1             \cf3 "South,09:00:00 AM 01/01/2026,20\\n"\cf1 )\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1         self.assertEqual(errors, [])\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1         self.assertEqual(set(observations), \{\cf3 "North"\cf1 , \cf3 "South"\cf1 \})\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1         self.assertEqual(observations[\cf3 "North"\cf1 ][\cf4 0\cf1 ][\cf4 1\cf1 ], -\cf4 12.5\cf1 )\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1     \cf5 def\cf1  test_chronological_sort(self) -> \cf5 None\cf1 :\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1         \cf3 """Sort across years and noon by datetime rather than date text."""\par
\pard\f1\fs17\b0\sl200\slmult0\sa0 \cf1         observations, _ = self.read(\par
